riticism, unorganized. Agent 1 argues B's strengths outweigh his uncooperativeness. Agent 3 also leans B.\n\nWe need to decide if we change vote. We could maintain C, but need to address concerns. We could ask for more info on C's teamwork, but we already asked and got no info. So we have no concrete evidence of C's teamwork. The concerns are multiple. B's uncooperativeness is also a concern but less specific. Which candidate is stronger overall? Both have concerns. B has strong reliability, stress, technical. C has leadership, anticipation, technical, but also multiple concerns. I think we might shift to B, acknowledging that the lack of concrete evidence for C's teamwork and the multiple concerns make B more reliable.\n\nThus we will change vote to Candidate B, providing reasoning: B's reliability, stress handling, technical competence, and we have no concrete evidence of C's teamwork, plus concerns about unfriendly, not open to new ideas, unorganized affect many criteria. So we now recommend B.\n\nWe must include explicit facts: B is very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills; concerns: can be grumpy, uncooperative. C: very good leadership, anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision; concerns: regarded as show-off, not open to new ideas, not good at taking criticism, unorganized.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 3's point and Agent 1's earlier. Provide our updated recommendation.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate B."}
